<div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px">
<p><strong>Verdict &mdash; High (7 / 10), and the shape of it is the point.</strong> Zee is <em>not</em> an earnings-manipulation case: the financial-statement core is clean &mdash; an unqualified audit, a clean CARO 2020, no restatement, and forensic screens that all read benign (detail in Pillar 5 and Annexure A3). The High rating is set entirely by the <strong>governance wrapper</strong> around those clean numbers &mdash; active regulatory enforcement, a control-without-ownership promoter structure, related-party value-leakage, and a heavy litigation load. On the financials alone Zee would sit in the Low band; it is the governance, related-party and enforcement layer that lifts it to High.</p>
<p class="override-note"><strong>Why 7 and not lower:</strong> an enforcement-tier override floors the composite at 7 on the active securities-account freeze plus the live SEBI proceeding; the confirmed-fraud tier does <em>not</em> fire, because those matters remain sub judice. The override sets a floor, not a ceiling &mdash; derivation in Annexure A4.</p>
</div>
<div class="sub-title">Key Issues at a Glance</div>
<ul class="glance">
<li class="g-crit"><strong>Regulatory enforcement</strong> &mdash; an active securities-account freeze and a live fund-diversion show-cause notice reaching the entity and its leadership.<span class="g-ptr">Pillar 6 &middot; corroborated in the post-period addendum (S1)</span></li>
<li class="g-high"><strong>Ownership &amp; control</strong> &mdash; promoter economic stake collapsed to a sliver while board and voting control persist: control without economic alignment.<span class="g-ptr">Pillar 2</span></li>
<li class="g-high"><strong>Related-party leakage</strong> &mdash; recurring value-leakage through a dense affiliate web, several events flagged in the auditor's Key Audit Matters.<span class="g-ptr">Pillar 3</span></li>
<li class="g-high"><strong>Litigation load</strong> &mdash; a large international arbitration and multiple insolvency petitions against the company.<span class="g-ptr">Pillar 6</span></li>
<li class="g-med"><strong>Board &amp; management stability</strong> &mdash; leadership transition and elevated director churn through the enforcement period.<span class="g-ptr">Pillars 1 &amp; 4</span></li>
<li class="g-low"><strong>Financials &amp; earnings quality &mdash; clean</strong> &mdash; benign forensic models, unqualified audit, cash-backed earnings; the sole watch is content-inventory valuation.<span class="g-ptr">Pillar 5</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="sub-title">Governance-Issue Sub-Scores</div>
<div class="kpi-row c4">
<div class="kpi t-med"><div class="kpi-lbl">Reliability</div><div class="kpi-val" style="font-size:16px;font-family:var(--font);color:#3A4400">Elevated · 5</div><div class="kpi-sub">CEO named in live SEBI fund-diversion SCN (alleged); recurring CSR shortfalls; clean guidance &amp; auditor otherwise</div></div>
<div class="kpi t-high"><div class="kpi-lbl">Fairness</div><div class="kpi-val" style="font-size:16px;font-family:var(--font);color:var(--high-text)">High · 7</div><div class="kpi-sub">Promoter 3.99% (control w/o stake); dense RPT network with documented value-leakage &amp; ICD arbitration</div></div>
<div class="kpi t-med"><div class="kpi-lbl">Effective Supervision</div><div class="kpi-val" style="font-size:16px;font-family:var(--font);color:#3A4400">Mixed · 4–5</div><div class="kpi-sub">Board independent &amp; refreshed, but 25 director exits (2.5:1); forensic accounting sound (4)</div></div>
<div class="kpi t-high"><div class="kpi-lbl">Transparency</div><div class="kpi-val" style="font-size:16px;font-family:var(--font);color:var(--high-text)">High · 8</div><div class="kpi-sub">Active NSDL freeze; live SEBI SCN; US$940 M arbitration; 8 insolvency petitions</div></div>
</div>
<div class="sub-title">GFA Six-Pillar Summary (Annexure P1 to P6)</div>
<table class="tbl"><thead><tr><th style="width:30px">#</th><th>Pillar</th><th style="width:150px">Rating</th><th>Headline &amp; sources</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td class="mono">1</td><td>Management practices</td><td><span class="badge med"><span class="dot med"></span>Elevated · 5</span></td><td>CEO Punit Goenka named in live SEBI fund-diversion SCN (12 Feb 2026) &amp; the set-aside 2023 interim bar — <strong>alleged, sub judice</strong>; FAM-PEP match. Recurring CSR shortfalls. Mitigants: unqualified audits, delivered filings, clean GST</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">2</td><td>Ownership &amp; history</td><td><span class="badge high"><span class="dot high"></span>High · 7</span></td><td>Promoter holding <strong>3.99%</strong> — control without economic stake; 100+ subsidiaries incl. Russia (OOO Zee CIS) &amp; multiple FZ-LLCs; back-history of Essel-group restructurings</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">3</td><td><strong>Related parties</strong></td><td><span class="badge high"><span class="dot high"></span>High · 7</span></td><td><strong>Core finding — governance pattern.</strong> Controlling family at 3.99% over a 100+ entity web; recurring affiliate value-leakage — a <strong>₹80.9 Cr Margo exceptional charge</strong> (₹37.2 Cr write-off + ₹43.7 Cr diminution) on an unfavourable guarantee arbitration, <strong>₹170.6 Cr ICDs in arbitration</strong>; ₹93.1 Cr ATL Media dividend supports standalone profit. Same channels feature in the SEBI fund-diversion allegations. Management asserts arm’s length (Ind AS 24)</td></tr>
