<div class="prose">
<p><strong>1.1 / 1.6 Management integrity &amp; live screening.</strong> CEO Punit Goenka is named in a <strong>live SEBI show-cause notice (12 Feb 2026)</strong> alleging fund diversion linked to the 2019 Yes Bank/FD matter, and in a June 2023 SEBI interim order that barred him from director/KMP roles for alleged siphoning via layered transactions. The interim bar was <strong>set aside by the SAT</strong>; the underlying investigation continued and culminated in the 2026 SCN. These are <strong>allegations under process, not adjudicated findings</strong> — the framework scores them as a reliability concern, not as confirmed misconduct (which would move P1 to 7–8 and trigger F-1). The Global Screening section returns a <strong>FAM-category PEP match</strong> on Goenka (100% name match), consistent with the Essel founding family; no sanctions or AML hits on the entity or principals.</p>
<p><strong>1.5 Reliability of the results narrative.</strong> Disconfirming the integrity concern: auditor opinions are unqualified across FY23–FY25, GST filing is fully compliant (3,464 records, nil delays), and there is no restatement or late-filing pattern. The reliability concern is <strong>governance-allegation-driven, not accounting-driven</strong>. Recurring CSR shortfalls (FY18–FY20, FY25; FY25 spend ₹11.4 Cr vs ₹22.7 Cr prescribed) are a statutory-discipline signal weighed here.</p>
</div>
