<p><strong>2.2 Ownership concentration and control.</strong> The defining feature is a <strong>promoter holding of 3.99%</strong> (3.83 Cr of 96.05 Cr shares) against 96.02% public float. For a founder-controlled media group this is <strong>structurally anomalous</strong>: the promoter family retains practical control and naming association while holding almost no economic stake — the alignment that normally disciplines a controlling shareholder is largely absent. This is the inverse of the usual Indian promoter-pledge risk (there is little stake left to pledge), but it raises the same governance question: control without proportionate economic exposure.</p>
<p><strong>2.3 Company history &amp; structure.</strong> Over 100 subsidiaries and step-downs across jurisdictions, including <strong>Russia-domiciled OOO Zee CIS Holding LLC / OOO Zee CIS LLC</strong> and multiple UAE FZ-LLCs (ATL Media FZ-LLC, Z5X Global FZ-LLC), within the legacy Essel-group lineage. The breadth of the consolidation perimeter and the related-party density (P3) are the avenues the framework is concerned with; the FY25 consolidated PAT (₹680 Cr) sitting below standalone PAT (₹701 Cr) confirms net subsidiary drag.</p>
