<div class="prose">
<p><strong>3.2 Affiliate flows — impact on profit and cash.</strong> The single most material item is a <strong>₹93.1 Cr dividend received from subsidiary ATL Media Limited</strong> in FY25 (nil in FY24). Standalone profit before tax was ₹906 Cr, so this related-party dividend is equivalent to <strong>roughly 10% of PBT</strong> — not the dominant driver, but a non-trivial intra-group contribution. It is properly disclosed; the point for a reader assessing earnings durability is that a portion of standalone profit is an <strong>intra-group distribution rather than third-party operating income</strong>.</p>
<p><strong>3.2 Value-leakage events.</strong> Two corroborated clusters, flagged in the auditor’s Key Audit Matters: (a) a single <strong>₹80.9 Cr Margo exceptional charge</strong>, recognised on an unfavourable arbitration over a guarantee invoked by a customer of subsidiary Margo Networks. Per Note 30 read with Note 32, this ₹809 M provision comprises <strong>₹37.2 Cr of balances written off</strong> plus a <strong>₹43.7 Cr provision for diminution</strong> in the Margo investment (₹372 M + ₹437 M = ₹809 M) — a single charge, not three separate ones; (b) <strong>₹170.6 Cr of inter-corporate deposits given to related parties, now the subject of arbitration</strong> for recovery. A second auditor KAM — recoverability of investment in subsidiaries carried at cost — reinforces the same affiliate-exposure concern. Together these are the documented channel through which affiliate exposure has crystallised into charges and disputes — the forensic substance behind the broader fund-diversion allegations, distinct from those allegations themselves.</p>
<p><strong>3.1 / 3.3 Recurring related-party cost base.</strong> Purchase of services from related parties runs ~<strong>₹320.6 Cr</strong> (ATL Media FZ-LLC ₹146.7 Cr, Asia Today ₹67.5 Cr, DSMCS ₹52.4 Cr, Z5X Global ₹54.8 Cr) plus purchase of media content from Zee Studios (₹71.9 Cr). These are recurring and material; the framework records them as a related-party dependency requiring arm’s-length substantiation (routed to analyst probe), not as confirmed extraction.</p>
</div>
