 Sans" fill="#16a34a" text-anchor="middle">avg firm</text><text x="0" y="178" font-size="10" font-family="DM Sans" fill="#99AFBC" font-style="italic">Beneish/Montier/Dechow (manipulation), Altman (distress), Piotroski (strength), Sloan (earnings quality) — deterministic, FY25 consolidated.</text></svg><div class="chart-cap">Unlike a high-growth or acquisitive firm (where these models over-flag), Zee’s revenue is flat-to-declining and the balance sheet is cash-rich and low-leverage — so the screens read clean on their own terms. Dechow is directional only (US-AAER calibrated; no Indian equivalent).</div></div>
