<div class="card-hdr"><div class="sec-title-grp"><span class="sec-num" id="p6">P6</span><div><div class="pillar-eyebrow">Governance issue · Transparency</div><span class="sec-title">Legal &amp; Regulatory</span></div></div><span class="badge high"><span class="dot high"></span>High · 8 / 10</span></div>
<div class="assess">Stakeholder interests with hidden ramifications for shareholder capital: regulatory disputes, legal and tax issues, contingent liabilities, and sanctions/enforcement exposure. Fed by D7 CDD §5 (screening), §6 (adverse media), §7 (regulatory) and §8 (litigation).</div>
<div class="prose">
<p><strong>6.2 Regulatory &amp; enforcement — active.</strong> The decisive matter is an <strong>active SEBI Whole-Time-Member-directed NSDL ISIN-level freeze</strong> (order WTM/AB/CFID/CFID_4/25884/2023-24) on the entity and on CFO M. V. Galgali, with PAN debarred for new accounts, returned TRUE_POSITIVE and operative as at the 19 May 2026 screening date — a current restriction, not a closed matter. Running alongside is the <strong>live SEBI show-cause notice (12 Feb 2026)</strong> alleging fund diversion (CEO and founder named), and a concluded SEBI <strong>settlement</strong> (₹7 lakh, 2019 pledged-share disclosure under PIT/SAST). The 2023 interim bar against the CEO was set aside by SAT. A SEBI insider-trading order (Mar 2023) implicated a senior employee in UPSI communication — an information-barrier control concern.</p>
<p><strong>6.1 Litigation &amp; contingencies.</strong> A <strong>US$940 M LCIA arbitration claim from Star/JioStar</strong> (Alliance Agreement terminated 20 Jun 2024; damages quantified at the 31 Aug 2024 proxy-award date at US$940 M plus costs and interest; Zee denies default, counterclaim US$8 m) is a material contingent exposure relative to a ~₹7,700 Cr revenue base. <strong>Eight active insolvency petitions</strong> (IDBI Bank 1071(MB)2025 &amp; Company Appeal(AT)(Ins)-939/2023; IndusInd C.P.(IB)-221/2022; IPRS C.P.(IB)-1279/2022) sit in NCLT/NCLAT; litigation dimension scored 9.0 in the CDD. Disputed indirect taxes aggregate ~₹273.5 Cr (including a ~₹173.6 Cr GST inadmissible-input-credit show-cause) and disputed direct taxes ~₹87.9 Cr (Note 35). CCI and an Invesco/OFI NCLT matter are <strong>disposed</strong> (recorded for completeness, low forward weight per §3.8).</p>
<p><strong>6.2 Sanctions/structural.</strong> No sanctions or AML hits on the entity or principals; however the <strong>Russia-domiciled OOO Zee CIS subsidiaries</strong> sit within an active EU/OFAC sanctions environment — a screening-and-compliance watch (D7 CDD §9), not a current hit. Zee is not a financial institution, limiting structural AML exposure.</p>
</div>
<div class="verdict-box"><div class="vscore"><div class="n" style="color:#6D3B00">8</div><div class="d">/10</div></div><div class="vtext"><b>High · 8.</b> Serious, active enforcement and contingency exposure: an operative SEBI-directed NSDL freeze, a live fund-diversion SCN, a US$940 M arbitration and eight insolvency petitions. Not 9–10 — the SEBI fraud matters are sub judice (no adjudicated finding; interim bar set aside), and the largest litigation items are contingent or disposed rather than crystallised penalties.</div></div>
